{"raw": {"https://jobs.lse.ac.uk/Vacancies/W/2722/0/474075/15539/assistant-professor-in-statistics": {"title": "Assistant Professor in Statistics", "description": "Assistant Professor in Statistics Register Login Back to search results Assistant Professor in Statistics LSE is committed to building a diverse, equitable and truly inclusive university As an equal opportunities employer strongly committed to equity, diversity and inclusion, we encourage applications from women and people from ethnic minority backgrounds as they are currently under-represented at this level in this area. All appointments will be made on merit or skill and experience relative to the role. Department of Statistics Assistant Professor in Statistics Salary is no less than \u00a368,087 per annum (pay award pending) and the salary scale can be found on the LSE website Applications for this new post are invited from outstanding candidates in the field of data science and statistics. Successful candidates will join an established and successful department and contribute to its research and teaching in data science and statistics. The post is tenable from 1 September 2027. You should have expertise and research interests in statistics, data science, or machine learning . You will have a track record or trajectory of internationally excellent publications, proven ability, as evidenced by existing publications, or potential to publish in top conferences or journals You will also have a clear, well-developed and viable strategy for future outstanding research that has the potential to result in world-leading publications. You must have a completed PhD, or close to obtaining a PhD in statistics or related areas such as computer science or mathematics by the post start date. The other criteria that will be used when shortlisting for this post can be found on the person specification, which is attached to this vacancy on the LSE\u2019s online recruitment system. We welcome applications from candidates who are keen to collaborate with colleagues with complementary research interests, both from within the Department and from other departments in the School. The Department has research expertise across different areas, including data science, probability in finance and insurance, social statistics, and time series and statistical learning. The School provides opportunities for research collaboration through the new Global Institute for Technology and Society, and other institutes. In addition to a competitive salary the benefits that come with this job include an occupational pension scheme, research grants policy with personal reward options, generous research leave (sabbatical) entitlement, a collegial faculty environment and excellent support, training and development opportunities. For further information about the post, please see the how to apply document , job description and the person specification. To apply for this post, please go to www.jobs.lse.ac.uk. If you have any technical queries with applying on the online system, please use the \u201ccontact us\u201d links at the bottom of the LSE Jobs page. Should you have any queries about the role, please email i.noble-andolfo@lse.ac.uk The closing date for receipt of applications is Sunday 13 December 2026 (23.59 UK time). W e are unable to accept any late applications. Apply now Back to search results Assistant Professor in Statistics Job Type: Academic Posted: 09/09/2026 Closing date: 13/12/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (GMT) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Baroness Baron Doctor Father Lady Lord Miss Mr Mrs Ms Professor Dame Professor Professor Lord Professor Sir Reverend Sir Other Dame Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection statement Create Account Cancel An email has been sent to your email address. Please confirm that your email address is active by clicking the link in the email. Powered by engage|ats Havas People a Havas Company This site is protected by reCAPTCHA. Contact Us - Application Query Terms and Conditions Privacy Policy Cookies Accessibility FAQs"}, "https://jobs.lse.ac.uk/Vacancies/W/3185/0/473672/15539/assistant-professor-in-international-development-quantitative-social-science": {"title": "Assistant Professor in International Development (Quantitative Social Science)", "description": "Assistant Professor in International Development (Quantitative Social Science) Register Login Back to search results Assistant Professor in International Development (Quantitative Social Science) LSE is committed to building a diverse, equitable and truly inclusive university As an equal opportunities employer strongly committed to diversity and inclusion, we\u00a0encourage applications from those of Minority Ethnic backgrounds and Women as they are currently under-represented at this level in this area. All appointments will be made on merit or skill and experience relative to the role. Department of International Development Assistant Professor in International Development (Quantitative Social Science) Salary is no less than \u00a368,087 per annum and the salary scale can be found on the LSE website The Department of International\u00a0Development invites applications for an Assistant Professor\u00a0in International Development (Quantitative Social Science). We are a vibrant multidisciplinary department seeking candidates with the potential to perform world-class research and teaching on contemporary development problems while working within and advancing social science disciplines. The successful candidate will teach students across all our MScs.\u00a0The successful candidate will be expected to conduct cutting-edge social science research on development using quantitative methods beyond mainstream economics, such as, for example, a strong disciplinary or multidisciplinary training in economic history, political science, sociology, anthropology, geography, statistics or data science relevant to international development. The role welcomes research addressing themes such as inequality, political stability and instability, governance, and technology and development. Ideally, candidates should have an interest in empirica lly grounded research with fieldwork-based research, and a desire to advance social science theory as evidenced by publications in highly rated social science and development journals or books. Successful applicants will have a PhD or be close to completing a PhD by the start date. They must show a commitment to working in a multidisciplinary environment and\u00a0contributing to the intellectual life of the School through conducting and publishing outstanding research, engaging in other high-quality teaching as instructed by the Head of Department (including Ph.D. training in time), and participating in the School and wider Departmental activities. The start date is 1 September 2027. Other criteria that will be used when shortlisting for this post can be found on the person specification, which is attached to this va cancy on the LSE\u2019s online recruitment system. In addition to a competitive salary, the benefits that come with this job include an occupational pension scheme, a research grants policy with personal reward options, generous research leave (sabbatical) entitlement, a collegial faculty environment, and excellent support, training and development opportunities. For further information about the post, please see the how to apply document , job description and the person specification . To apply for this post, please go to www.jobs.lse.ac.uk . If you have any technical queries with applying on the online system, please use the \u201ccontact us\u201d links at the bottom of the LSE Jobs page. Queries about research and teaching in the department may be directed to j.p.faguet@lse.ac.uk. The closing date for receipt of applications is 1 December 2026 (23.59 UK time). W e are unable to accept any late applications. Apply now Back to search results Assistant Professor in International Development (Quantitative Social Science) Job Type: Academic Posted: 01/09/2026 Closing date: 01/12/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (GMT) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Baroness Baron Doctor Father Lady Lord Miss Mr Mrs Ms Professor Dame Professor Professor Lord Professor Sir Reverend Sir Other Dame Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection statement Create Account Cancel An email has been sent to your email address. Please confirm that your email address is active by clicking the link in the email. Powered by engage|ats Havas People a Havas Company This site is protected by reCAPTCHA. Contact Us - Application Query Terms and Conditions Privacy Policy Cookies Accessibility FAQs"}, "https://jobs.lse.ac.uk/Vacancies/W/2933/0/473666/15539/assistant-professor-in-international-development": {"title": "Assistant Professor in International Development", "description": "Assistant Professor in International Development Register Login Back to search results Assistant Professor in International Development LSE is committed to building a diverse, equitable and truly inclusive university As an equal opportunities employer strongly committed to equity, diversity and inclusion, we encourage applications from women and people from ethnic minority backgrounds as they are currently under-represented at this level in this area. All appointments will be made on merit or skill and experience relative to the role. Department of International Development Assistant Professor in International Development Salary is no less than \u00a368,087 per annum and the salary scale can be found on the LSE website The Department of International\u00a0Development invites applications for an Assistant Professor\u00a0in International Development. We are a vibrant multidisciplinary department seeking candidates with the potential to perform world-class research and teaching on contemporary development problems while working within and advancing social science disciplines. The successful candidate will teach students across the department, and especially our MSc in International Development and Humanitarian Emergencies and MSc. Development Studies.\u00a0They will have a background in Anthropology, Political Science, Sociology, or related disciplines. We especially welcome applicants with a research interest in the causes, consequences, and responses to conflict, violence, and crisis in the Global South, including themes such as social vulnerability and access to livelihoods, food security and hunger, gender, state capacity, environmental risks, and the political economy of crisis responses in an era of cuts to development aid. Ideally, candidates should have experience of empirical fieldwork-based research, and a desire to advance social science theory as evidenced by publications in highly rated social science and development journals or books. Successful applicants will have a PhD, or be close to completing a PhD by the start date. They must show a commitment to working in a multidisciplinary environment and\u00a0contributing to the intellectual life of the School through conducting and publishing outstanding research, engaging in other high-quality teaching as instructed by the Head of Department (including Ph.D. training in time), and participating in the School and wider Departmental activities. The start date is 1 September 2027. The other criteria that will be used when shortlisting for this post can be found on the person specification, which is attached to this vacancy on the LSE\u2019s online recruitment system. In addition to a competitive salary the benefits that come with this job include an occupational pension scheme, a research grants policy with personal reward options, generous research leave (sabbatical) entitlement, a collegial faculty environment and excellent support, training and development opportunities. For further information about the post, please see the how to apply document , job description and the person specification . To apply for this post, please go to www.jobs.lse.ac.uk . If you have any technical queries with applying on the online system, please use the \u201ccontact us\u201d links at the bottom of the LSE Jobs page. Should you have any queries about the role, please email p.faguet@lse.ac.uk. The closing date for receipt of applications is 1 December 2026 (23.59 UK time). W e are unable to accept any late applications. Apply now Back to search results Assistant Professor in International Development Job Type: Academic Posted: 01/09/2026 Closing date: 01/12/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (GMT) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Baroness Baron Doctor Father Lady Lord Miss Mr Mrs Ms Professor Dame Professor Professor Lord Professor Sir Reverend Sir Other Dame Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection statement Create Account Cancel An email has been sent to your email address. Please confirm that your email address is active by clicking the link in the email. Powered by engage|ats Havas People a Havas Company This site is protected by reCAPTCHA. Contact Us - Application Query Terms and Conditions Privacy Policy Cookies Accessibility FAQs"}, "https://jobs.lse.ac.uk/Vacancies/W/3772/0/475572/15539/head-of-randi-assessment-and-intelligence": {"title": "Head of R&I Assessment & Intelligence", "description": "Head of R&I Assessment & Intelligence Register Login Back to search results Head of R&I Assessment & Intelligence LSE is committed to building a diverse, equitable and truly inclusive university Research & Innovation Head of R&I Assessment & Intelligence Salary from \u00a3\u00a363,370 to \u00a3\u00a373,163 pa inclusive with potential to progress to \u00a3\u00a380,927 pa inclusive of London allowance LSE is a leading social science institution with huge global impact. Our researchers are world-leading thinkers on critical issues, and our mission is to know the causes of things for the betterment of society. LSE Research and Innovation helps to develop and sustain an environment that makes LSE the best place in the world to do excellent and impactful social science research. The R&I Assessment & Intelligence team brings together a multi-faceted service that aims to help understand, reflect and advise on the changing internal and external expectations on LSE for its research and innovation activities. This includes the provision of research intelligence to improve LSE\u2019s ability to respond to the external environment, strengthening research excellence and preparing for institutional exercises such as the REF assessment exercise, overseeing the management of allocated block funding and the subsequent infrastructure around the optimum use of internal funding, and engaging with senior stakeholders to support institutional decision-making. The postholder will provide senior professional leadership for the team, ensuring that its work is coherent, well governed and translated into clear timely strategic advice, effective delivery and practical support for senior institutional decision-making and successful performance delivery against LSE ambitions and priorities. Candidates should have: Senior leadership experience in a research-intensive environment, including leading institutional preparations for REF. Expertise in research intelligence, quantitative and qualitative analysis, evaluation and critical thinking, including the responsible use of AI, to inform senior decision-making. Excellent written, oral and interpersonal skills, with the ability to communicate complex or sensitive information clearly and build effective relationships with senior stakeholders. Strong strategic planning, collaboration and change-management skills, including establishing effective governance, workplans, resource plans, risk controls and progress monitoring. A proven commitment to high-quality service delivery, with experience of improving integrated services, systems, processes, communications and knowledge management through innovative problem-solving. We offer an occupational pension scheme, generous annual leave, hybrid working, and excellent training and development opportunities. For further information about the post, please see the how to apply document , job description and the person specification . To apply for this post, please go to www.jobs.lse.ac.uk . If you have any technical queries with applying on the online system, please use the \u201ccontact us\u201d links at the bottom of the LSE Jobs page. Should you have any queries about the role, please email g.mcconnell@lse.ac.uk . The closing date for receipt of applications is 15 th November 2026 (23.59 UK time). Regrettably, we are unable to accept any late applications. Apply now Back to search results Head of R&I Assessment & Intelligence Job Type: Professional Services Posted: 09/10/2026 Closing date: 15/11/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (GMT) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Baroness Baron Doctor Father Lady Lord Miss Mr Mrs Ms Professor Dame Professor Professor Lord Professor Sir Reverend Sir Other Dame Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection statement Create Account Cancel An email has been sent to your email address. Please confirm that your email address is active by clicking the link in the email. Powered by engage|ats Havas People a Havas Company This site is protected by reCAPTCHA. Contact Us - Application Query Terms and Conditions Privacy Policy Cookies Accessibility FAQs By clicking \u201cAccept All Cookies\u201d, you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to enhance site navigation, analyze site usage, and assist in our marketing efforts. View our privacy policy Cookies Settings Reject All Accept All Cookies Privacy Preference Center When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. This information might be about you, your preferences or your device and is mostly used to make the site work as you expect it to. The information does not usually directly identify you, but it can give you a more personalized web experience. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. Click on the different category headings to find out more and change our default settings. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Allow All Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Services Always Active These Services are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. Functional Services Functional Services With these services, the website is able to provide advanced functionality and personalization. They may be set by us or by third parties whose services we use on our sites. If you do not allow these services, this website may not function properly. Back Button Cookie List Search Icon Filter Icon Clear checkbox label label Apply Cancel Consent Leg.Interest checkbox label label checkbox label label checkbox label label Reject All Confirm My Choices 1 Technical Support Today New Messages Technical Support Chatbot (with creds) a few seconds ago Welcome to Technical Support. Please could you let us know whether you're a candidate or a recruiter? Candidate Recruiter \u26a1 by Freshworks 1"}, "https://jobs.lse.ac.uk/Vacancies/W/1939/0/473549/15539/planning-officer-power-bi-developer": {"title": "Planning Officer (Power BI Developer)", "description": "Planning Officer (Power BI Developer) Register Login Back to search results Planning Officer (Power BI Developer) LSE is committed to building a diverse, equitable and truly inclusive university Planning Division Planning Officer (Power BI Developer) Salary from \u00a343,277 to \u00a351,714 pa inclusive with potential to progress to \u00a355,497 pa inclusive of London allowance This is fixed term for one year The London School of Economics and Political Science is one of the foremost social science universities in the world. The Planning Division is integral in supporting and monitoring the School\u2019s progress towards achieving its strategic objectives. The Planning Officer (Power BI Developer) supports a range of tasks undertaken across the School, primarily relating to the production of Power BI reports, dashboards and applications to support insight and strategic decision making across the School. Candidates should have: Experience designing and maintaining high\u2011quality visualisation reports, dashboards and applications. Experience of ETL processes using Alteryx, PowerQuery (M) or Fabric tools (e.g. Dataflows, Lakehouse, pipelines) to create reliable datasets for reporting. Experience developing and managing robust semantic models (dimensional/star schema) to underpin scalable and reusable reporting solutions including DAX optimisation and model design best practice. Experience working with end-users and stakeholders to translate business requirements into data models, measures and visualisations that deliver actionable insights. Ability to relate to and work with technical and non-technical staff at every level of the School. Ability to provide training and support to peers and end-users in-person and online. We offer an occupational pension scheme, generous annual leave, hybrid working, and excellent training and development opportunities. For further information about the post, please see the how to apply document , job description and the person specification . To apply for this post, please go to www.jobs.lse.ac.uk . If you have any technical queries with applying on the online system, please use the \u201ccontact us\u201d links at the bottom of the LSE Jobs page. Should you have any queries about the role, please email Planning.Division@lse.ac.uk . The closing date for receipt of applications is 15 November 2026\u00a0(23.59 UK time). Regrettably, we are unable to accept any late applications. Apply now Back to search results Planning Officer (Power BI Developer) Job Type: Professional Services Posted: 07/10/2026 Closing date: 15/11/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (GMT) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Baroness Baron Doctor Father Lady Lord Miss Mr Mrs Ms Professor Dame Professor Professor Lord Professor Sir Reverend Sir Other Dame Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email a