ces, the website is able to provide advanced functionality and personalization. They may be set by us or by third parties whose services we use on our sites. If you do not allow these services, this website may not function properly. Back Button Cookie List Search Icon Filter Icon Clear checkbox label label Apply Cancel Consent Leg.Interest checkbox label label checkbox label label checkbox label label Reject All Confirm My Choices 1 Technical Support Today New Messages Technical Support Chatbot (with creds) a few seconds ago Welcome to Technical Support. Please could you let us know whether you're a candidate or a recruiter? Candidate Recruiter \u26a1 by Freshworks 1"}, "https://jobs.lse.ac.uk/Vacancies/W/6558/0/473609/15539/assistant-professor-in-finance": {"title": "Assistant Professor in Finance", "description": "Assistant Professor in Finance Register Login Back to search results Assistant Professor in Finance LSE is committed to building a diverse, equitable and truly inclusive university As an equal opportunities employer strongly committed to diversity and inclusion, we\u00a0encourage applications from women and those of Ethnic Minority backgrounds as they are currently under-represented at this level in this area. All appointments will be made on merit or skill and experience relative to the role. Department of Finance Assistant Professor in Finance Salary is competitive with Departments at our peer institutions worldwide. Applications are invited from outstanding candidates for one or more career-track Assistant Professor in Finance positions. You will carry out research and teach at the undergraduate and postgraduate level. Candidates should have a completed PhD, or be close to obtaining a PhD, in finance or economics by the position start date. In addition, candidates should possess expertise and research interests in finance and demonstrate a clear, well developed, and viable strategy for future outstanding research that has the potential to result in world-leading publications. You will also be able to demonstrate excellent written and oral communication skills, including an ability to place your specialised work within a broader social science context. The ability to teach finance at both the undergraduate and postgraduate level is essential. For near post-doctoral candidates, or candidates with limited post-doctoral experience, you will be able to demonstrate a developing record of research with potential for publication in leading peer-reviewed journals in finance. For post-doctoral candidates, you will be able to demonstrate a track record or trajectory of internationally excellent publications. The other criteria that will be used when shortlisting for this position can be found on the person specification, which is attached to this vacancy on the LSE\u2019s online recruitment system. In addition to a competitive salary the benefits that come with this job include an occupational pension scheme, a research grants policy with personal reward options, generous research leave (sabbatical) entitlement, a collegial faculty environment and excellent support, training and development opportunities. For further information about the post, please see the how to apply document , job description and the person specification . To apply for this post, please go to www.jobs.lse.ac.uk . If you have any technical queries with applying on the online system, please use the \u201ccontact us\u201d links at the bottom of the LSE Jobs page. Should you have any queries about the role, please email finance.teachingmanager@lse.ac.uk . The closing date for receipt of applications is 13 November 2026 (23.59 UK time). W e are unable to accept any late applications. We will be conducting online first stage interviews in early December 2026, and final round interviews and seminars will be held on campus during January and February 2027. Apply now Back to search results Assistant Professor in Finance Job Type: Academic Posted: 01/09/2026 Closing date: 13/11/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (GMT) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Baroness Baron Doctor Father Lady Lord Miss Mr Mrs Ms Professor Dame Professor Professor Lord Professor Sir Reverend Sir Other Dame Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection statement Create Account Cancel An email has been sent to your email address. Please confirm that your email address is active by clicking the link in the email. Powered by engage|ats Havas People a Havas Company This site is protected by reCAPTCHA. Contact Us - Application Query Terms and Conditions Privacy Policy Cookies Accessibility FAQs"}, "https://jobs.lse.ac.uk/Vacancies/W/6834/0/474984/15539/assistant-professor-in-accounting": {"title": "Assistant Professor in Accounting", "description": "Assistant Professor in Accounting Register Login Back to search results Assistant Professor in Accounting LSE is committed to building a diverse, equitable and truly inclusive university As an equal opportunities employer strongly committed to diversity and inclusion, we\u00a0encourage applications from women and those of Minority Ethnic backgrounds as they are currently under-represented at this level in this area. All appointments will be made on merit or skill and experience relative to the role. Department of Accounting Assistant Professor in Accounting The Department of Accounting at LSE invites applications from outstanding candidates for the post of Assistant Professor in Accounting. Those specialising in any area of accounting are encouraged to apply, although when making recruiting decisions we will take into account teaching needs and priority areas as the ongoing development of the department and composition of the faculty may require. For further information on the department, see https://www.lse.ac.uk/accounting/about-us . Candidates will have: \u00b7 A completed PhD, or be close to obtaining a PhD, in accounting, or related area, by the post start date . \u00b7 A clear, well developed and viable strategy for outstanding research that has the potential to result in leading publications in accounting. \u00b7 Ability to teach accounting at under- and post-graduate level, ideally evidenced by prior experience in teaching. Further specific criteria that will be used when shortlisting for this post can be found on the person specification, which is attached to this vacancy on the LSE\u2019s online recruitment system. Candidates will also be expected to make relevant service and citizenship contributions as appropriate for early-career colleagues. The appointment is expected to commence no later than 1 September 2027. In addition to a competitive salary the benefits that come with this job include an occupational pension scheme, a research grants policy with personal reward options, generous research leave (sabbatical) entitlement, a collegial faculty environment and excellent support, training and development opportunities. For further information about the post, please see the How-to-Apply document , job description and the person specification . To apply for this post, please go to www.jobs.lse.ac.uk . If you have any technical queries about applying via the online system, please use the \u201ccontact us\u201d links at the bottom of the LSE Jobs page. If you have queries about the role, please email the Department Manager, Yvonne Guthrie ( y.guthrie@lse.ac.uk ) . The closing date for receipt of applications is 6 November 2026 (23.59 UK time). We are unable to accept any late applications. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to give a presentation and meet with the faculty. Apply now Back to search results Assistant Professor in Accounting Job Type: Academic Posted: 28/09/2026 Closing date: 06/11/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (GMT) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Baroness Baron Doctor Father Lady Lord Miss Mr Mrs Ms Professor Dame Professor Professor Lord Professor Sir Reverend Sir Other Dame Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection statement Create Account Cancel An email has been sent to your email address. Please confirm that your email address is active by clicking the link in the email. Powered by engage|ats Havas People a Havas Company This site is protected by reCAPTCHA. Contact Us - Application Query Terms and Conditions Privacy Policy Cookies Accessibility FAQs"}, "https://jobs.lse.ac.uk/Vacancies/W/1996/0/475539/15539/country-economist-jordan": {"title": "Country Economist Jordan", "description": "Country Economist Jordan Register Login Back to search results Country Economist Jordan LSE is committed to building a diverse, equitable and truly inclusive university. The International Growth Centre (IGC) Country Economist Jordan Salaries will be commensurate with experience, taking into account pay equity within the Centre. Salary is no less than \u00a350,000 gross per annum plus 10% of retirement contribution supplement and inclusive of allowances The International Growth Centre (IGC) works with policymakers in developing countries to promote inclusive and sustainable growth through pathbreaking research. We are a global research centre with a network of world-leading researchers and in-country teams and initiatives working across Africa, South Asia, and the Middle East. Based at LSE and in partnership with the University of Oxford, Addis Ababa University (AAU) and the Lahore University of Management Sciences (LUMS), we are majority funded by the UK Foreign, Commonwealth and Development Office (FCDO). We work to improve the productivity of people and firms as the key driver of sustainable economic development. The IGC has embedded Country Economists in its partner countries which currently include Bangladesh, Ethiopia, India, Jordan, Mozambique, Pakistan, Sierra Leone and Zambia, as well as Flexible Engagement programmes including the Caribbean, Tanzania, Nepal and South Africa. The IGC is currently seeking a Country Economist or Country Economist Jordan based in Amman. Country Economists are a key part of the IGC\u2019s in-country presence, working under the leadership of the Country Director and Lead Academic to deliver the country strategy and connect local policy priorities with global research expertise. The role combines policy engagement, analytical work and programme delivery: building strong relationships with government, researchers, development partners and other stakeholders; identifying and supporting policy-relevant research opportunities; producing high-quality policy analysis and written outputs; and helping translate research into policy influence through meetings, events and wider communications. Country Economists also contribute to the effective management, monitoring and evaluation of the country programme, ensuring that activities remain responsive to local priorities and contribute to meaningful policy impact. Applicants should have strong economics skills, excellent quantitative skills in economic analysis, a sophisticated understanding of economic policy, and hold a post-graduate degree in economics, public policy, or a related discipline. Successful applicants will be dynamic self-starters with excellent written and oral communication skills. They will also demonstrate a team-oriented, respectful and collaborative approach to working with others. Fluency in Arabic is required. For further information about the posts, please see the how to apply document , CE job description and person specification . To apply for this post, please go to https://jobs.lse.ac.uk/ . If you have any technical queries with applying on the online system, please use the \u201ccontact us\u201d links at the bottom of the LSE Jobs page. If you have queries about the role, please email Vivian Bronsoler Nurko on v.bronsoler-nurko@lse.ac.uk To find out more about the position and International Growth Centre, please go to https://www.theigc.org/about/careers/ The closing date for applications is 30 October 2026 (23.59 UK time). Regrettably, we are unable to accept late applications. Apply now Back to search results Country Economist Jordan Job Type: Professional Services Posted: 09/10/2026 Closing date: 30/10/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (GMT) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Baroness Baron Doctor Father Lady Lord Miss Mr Mrs Ms Professor Dame Professor Professor Lord Professor Sir Reverend Sir Other Dame Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection statement Create Account Cancel An email has been sent to your email address. Please confirm that your email address is active by clicking the link in the email. Powered by engage|ats Havas People a Havas Company This site is protected by reCAPTCHA. Contact Us - Application Query Terms and Conditions Privacy Policy Cookies Accessibility FAQs By clicking \u201cAccept All Cookies\u201d, you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to enhance site navigation, analyze site usage, and assist in our marketing efforts. View our privacy policy Cookies Settings Reject All Accept All Cookies Privacy Preference Center When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. This information might be about you, your preferences or your device and is mostly used to make the site work as you expect it to. The information does not usually directly identify you, but it can give you a more personalized web experience. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. Click on the different category headings to find out more and change our default settings. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Allow All Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Services Always Active These Services are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. Functional Services Functional Services With these services, the website is able to provide advanced functionality and personalization. They may be set by us or by third parties whose services we use on our sites. If you do not allow these services, this website may not function properly. Back Button Cookie List Search Icon Filter Icon Clear checkbox label label Apply Cancel Consent Leg.Interest checkbox label label checkbox label label checkbox label label Reject All Confirm My Choices 1 Technical Support Today New Messages Technical Support Chatbot (with creds) a few seconds ago Welcome to Technical Support. Please could you let us know whether you're a candidate or a recruiter? Candidate Recruiter \u26a1 by Freshworks 1"}, "https://jobs.lse.ac.uk/Vacancies/W/1066/0/474023/15539/business-applications-specialist": {"title": "Business Applications Specialist", "description": "Business Applications Specialist Register Login Back to search results Business Applications Specialist LSE is committed to building a diverse, equitable and truly inclusive university Data and Technology Services Business Applications Specialist Salary from \u00a353,949 pa to \u00a362,160 pa inclusive with potential to progress to \u00a369,073 pa inclusive of London allowance This is a fixed term appointment for one year The London School of Economics is a cosmopolitan university situated in the vibrant centre of London specialising in the study of social sciences. Our Data and Technology Services division provides services to 14,000 staff and student users. Working with product owners and other team members to maintain and optimise business applications throughout the service life cycle ensuring continual service improvement. They will support reporting tools and systems to enable accurate management reporting as well as the incident management of issues relating to integrations between applications and database services. They will take the lead on maintenance projects, subject matter expertise and third line support within the maintenance and operational plans for systems related to application services, integrations between databases and applications and reporting infrastructure. Initially this role will focus on implementation of LSEs digital experience platform for first 12 months. Working as part of the Product/Project team acting as technical lead within the Digital Communications team and external partner to ensure the successful delivery of a school Intranet. The Business Application Specialist will: Work closely with service owners to understand application roadmaps ensuring best value from available products Ensure continual service improvement through in particular: - Automation of repetitive support tasks - Remote management of systems to monitor performance and respond to alerts - Devolving support tasks to front line services or service lines to improve efficiency of the service - Identifying opportunities for enhancing productivity and the user experience - Ensure maintained services are patched and secure according to required security standards (Cyber Essentials +) where applicable Maintain reference documentation such as schematics, technical guidelines, operational standards and details of IT assets Provide subject matter expertise on business application services to the LSE, including providing technical expertise to support decision making Candidates should have: Experience with managing server and software configurations including Apache/Tomcat/SSL Certificates/IIS etc. Knowledge of the install upgrade maintenance and support of third-party applications, supporting business functions such as HR, Finance and Student Lifecycle Management Ability to utilise scripting languages and tools (e.g., Javascript, CSS/HTML, Python, PowerShell) Evidence of a strong technical background relating to industry standard technology (Linux/Windows/MS SQL/Oracle) Ability to communicate complex ideas and technical issues to a range of different non-technical audiences. Able to interpret user requirements offering solutions that offer an exceptional user experience and meet business needs Able to plan own work and deliver effective, agreed outcomes as per scheduled. We offer an occupational pension scheme, generous annual leave, hybrid working, and excellent training and development opportunities. For further information about the post, please see the how to apply document , job description and the person specification . To apply for this post, please go to www.jobs.lse.ac.uk . If you have any technical queries with applying on the online system, please use the \u201ccontact us\u201d links at the bottom of the LSE Jobs page. Should you have any queries about the role, please email dts.admin@lse.ac.uk . The closing date for receipt of applications is 26 October 2026 (23.59 UK time). Regrettably, we are unable to accept any late applications. Apply now Back to search results Business Applications Specialist Job Type: Professional Services Posted: 09/10/2026 Closing date: 26/10/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (GMT) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Baroness Baron Doctor Father Lady Lord Miss Mr Mrs Ms Professor Dame Professor Professor Lord Professor Sir Reverend Sir Other Dame Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection statement Create Account Cancel An email has been sent to your email address. Please confirm that your email address is active by clicking the link in the email. Powered by engage|ats Havas People a Havas Company This site is protected by reCAPTCHA. Contact Us - Application Query Terms and Conditions Privacy Policy Cookies Accessibility FAQs"}, "https://jobs.lse.ac.uk/Vacancies/W/5219/0/475307/15539/grant-application-manager-innovation-and-impact": {"title": "Grant Application Manager (Innovation & Impact)", "description": "Grant Application Manager (Innovation & Impact) Register Login Back to search results Grant Application Manager (Innovation & Impact) LSE is committed to building a diverse, equitable and truly inclusive university Research & Innovation Grant Application Manager (Innovation & Impact) Salary from \u00a343,277 to \u00a351,714 pa inclusive with potential to progress to \u00a355,497 pa inclusive of London allowance This role is offered on an initial 6-month basis, with potential to extend. It is a full-time appointment, working 35 hours per week. Flexible and part-time working arrangements will be considered, subject to business needs. This role can be offered as a secondment\nopportunity for internal staff. We are pleased to invite applications to this role with LSE\u2019s Innovation & Impact (I&I) team, based in the School\u2019s Research & Innovation Division, which provides wide-ranging support to help make LSE the best place in the world to do excellent and impactful research. The Grant Application Manager (I&I) will play an integral role in the continued work of the Innovation & Impact team to maximise the impacts of LSE research through a wide range of activities and pathways, including research commercialisation. To that end, the Grant Application Manager (I&I) will provide professional pre-award support for the development and submission of innovation and impact-focused funding applications. They will manage eligibility checks, costing and pricing, budget development and submission preparation to ensure timely, accurate and compliant proposals to UK and international funders, as well as to LSE\u2019s internal innovation and impact funding schemes. Candidates should: Be educated to degree level or equivalent qualification, or equivalent professional experience. Have experience of supporting costing and pricing, funder regulations, and the development and submission of applications to a range of sponsors and funding bodies. Demonstrate excellent written and oral communication skills, including the ability to convey complex information effectively and confidently at all levels and to different audiences. Be able to prioritise actions and respond to competing demands in a complex environment. We welcome applications from LSE colleagues interested in this as a secondment role, as well as from candidates outside the School. You\u2019ll be joining a friendly and dynamic team with deep expertise and wide-ranging experience in maximising and optimising research impact and innovation, and with a strong focus on providing outstanding professional support to researchers across LSE. We offer an occupational pension scheme, generous annual leave, hybrid working, and excellent training and development opportunities. For further information about the post, please see the how to apply document , job description and the person specification . To apply for this post, please go to www.jobs.lse.ac.uk . If you have any technical queries with applying on the online system, please use the \u201ccontact us\u201d links at the bottom of the LSE Jobs page. Should you have any queries about the role, please email Rachel Middlemass at R.Middlemass@lse.ac.uk . The closing date for receipt of applications is Sunday 25 October 2026 (23.59 UK time). Regrettably, we are unable to accept any late applications. Apply now Back to search results Grant Application Manager (Innovation & Impact) Job Type: Professional Services Posted: 05/10/2026 Closing date: 25/10/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (GMT) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Baroness Baron Doctor Father Lady Lord Miss Mr Mrs Ms Professor Dame Professor Professor Lord Professor Sir Reverend Sir Other Dame Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection statement Create Account Cancel An email has been sent to your email address. Please confirm that your email address is active by clicking the link in the email. Powered by engage|ats Havas People a Havas Company This site is protected by reCAPTCHA. Contact Us - Application Query Terms and Conditions Privacy Policy Cookies Accessibility FAQs By clicking \u201cAccept All Cookies\u201d, you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to enhance site navigation, analyze site usage, and assist in our marketing efforts. View our privacy policy Cookies Settings Reject All Accept All Cookies Privacy Preference Center When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. This information might be about you, your preferences or your device and is mostly used to make the site work as you expect it to. The information does not usually directly identify you, but it can give you a more personalized web experience. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. Click on the different category headings to find out more and change our default settings. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Allow All Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Services Always Active These Services are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. Functional Services Functional Services With these services, the website is able to provide advanced functionality and personalization. They may be set by us or by third parties whose services we use on our sites. If you do not allow these services, this website may not function properly. Back Button Cookie List Search Icon Filter Icon Clear checkbox label label Apply Cancel Consent Leg.Interest checkbox label label checkbox label label checkbox label label Reject All Confirm My Choices 1 Technical Support Today New Messages Technical Support Chatbot (with creds) a few seconds ago Welcome to Technical Support. Please could you let us know whether you're a candidate or a recruiter? Candidate Recruiter \u26a1 by Freshworks 1"}, "https://jobs.lse.ac.uk/Vacancies/W/3446/0/474866/15539/distinguished-policy-fellow-cetex-director-emde-private-capital-mobilisation-and-fiscal-policy": {"title": "Distinguished Policy Fellow (CETEx Director)", "description": "Distinguished Policy Fellow (CETEx Director) \u2013 EMDE Private Capital Mobilisation & Fiscal Policy Register Login Back to search results Distinguished Policy Fellow (CETEx Director) \u2013 EMDE Private Capital Mobilisation & Fiscal Policy LSE is committed to building a diverse, equitable and truly inclusive university Centre for Economic Transition Expertise Distinguished Policy Fellow (CETEx Director) \u2013 EMDE Private Capital Mobilisation & Fiscal Policy Salary from \u00a374,224 to \u00a394,861 pa inclusive of London allowance Funding for this appointment is available for 3 years. The Global School of Sustainability has established a new Centre for Economic Transition Expertise (CETEx), focused on leveraging, strengthening and amplifying research, and developing well targeted policy analysis and other outputs, by convening policymakers, and by providing technical support, assistance and capacity-building. This new centre will support the reforms necessary to deliver sustainable, inclusive and resilient economies and financial systems around the world. CETEx is seeking to appoint a Distinguished Policy Fellow (Director) to lead programmes with respect to private capital mobilisation (PCM), economic and fiscal policies in emerging markets and development economies (EMDE), with a geographic focus on China and Latin America, and related capacity-building programmes, as well as multilateral engagements with respect to PCM, fiscal and debt sustainability in EMDEs. The post-holder will lead CETEx\u2019s work on mobilising private capital for climate transition across advanced and emerging economies, driving innovative approaches to blended finance, development banking, investment structures, credit methodologies, and international policy frameworks that accelerate capital flows for net zero. The role will also oversee CETEx\u2019s economic and fiscal policy programmes in emerging markets, aligning fiscal policy, investment, and catalytic capital to support sustainable economic transition. Candidates will have a Master\u2019s degree in economics, finance, public policy, development studies, or a closely related field, with substantive senior\u2011level professional experience gained in government, international organisations, development finance institutions, or global finance. The post-holder will hold demonstrated track record of developing and delivering policy in a national or sub-national government or international organisation in one or more of the following areas: blended finance/private capital mobilisation, fiscal policy, or international development. Furthermore, candidates should have a solid track record of producing or overseeing the production of outstanding, research\u2011based, policy-relevant outputs that have demonstrably influenced public debate and decision-making at senior levels, and extensive experience overseeing the conduct of complex analytical and policy work\u2014including global stocktakes, assessments of international initiatives, and analysis of structural barriers to mobilisation (e.g., prudential regulation, trade/subsidy policy, investment structures). We offer an occupational pension scheme, generous annual leave, hybrid working, and excellent training and development opportunities. For further information about the post, please see the how to apply document , job description and the person specification . If you have any technical queries with applying on the online system, please use the \u201ccontact us\u201d links at the bottom of the LSE Jobs page. Should you have any queries about the role, please email gri.hr@lse.ac.uk The closing date for receipt of applications is 21 October 2026 (23.59 UK time). Regrettably, we are unable to accept any late applications. Apply now Back to search results Distinguished Policy Fellow (CETEx Director) \u2013 EMDE Private Capital Mobilisation & Fiscal Policy Job Type: Policy Posted: 24/09/2026 Closing date: 21/10/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (BST) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Baroness Baron Doctor Father Lady Lord Miss Mr Mrs Ms Professor Dame Professor Professor Lord Professor Sir Reverend Sir Other Dame Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection statement Create Account Cancel An email has been sent to your email address. Please confirm that your email address is active by clicking the link in the email. Powered by engage|ats Havas People a Havas Company This site is protected by reCAPTCHA. Contact Us - Application Query Terms and Conditions Privacy Policy Cookies Accessibility FAQs"}, "https://jobs.lse.ac.uk/Vacancies/W/4179/0/475329/15539/research-assistant": {"title": "Research Assistant", "description": "Research Assistant Register Login Back to search results Research Assistant LSE is committed to building a diverse, equitable and truly inclusive university Management Research Assistant Salary from \u00a336,513 to \u00a341,565 pa inclusive with potential to progress to \u00a344,468 pa inclusive of London allowance Funding is available to support this position for 12 months The post supports a research programme lead by Dr. Ra\u00fal S\u00e1nchez De La Sierra from LSE\u2019s Department of Management. The research programme concerns armed groups, state formation, and governance in the eastern De mocratic Republic of Congo. This is a field-intensive post. The post holder will spend roughly half of each year in North and South Kivu, including in remote artisanal mining areas several hours or days from the nearest town, reached by motorbike or on foot. Main duties and responsibilities include identifying appropriate methods of investigation or analysis according to data and objectives; conveying complex conceptual ideas or complex information which may be highly detailed, technical or specialist; interpreting and analysing patterns or trends in data; managing large scale databases. Candidates should have a completed Master or Bachelor\u2019s degree (or equivalent) in economics or other closely related quantitative discipline; graduate degree in economics or public policy that includes graduate level coursework in econometrics as well as in political economy, or Maters-level economics research training; knowledge of the research literature on the political economy of conflict and armed group governance; experience in cleaning and managing large survey and administrative datasets; proficiency in Stata, R, or Python; resilience to work for extended periods in a remote insecure setting . We offer an occupational pension scheme, generous annual leave, hybrid working, and excellent training and development opportunities. For further information about the post, please see the how to apply document , job description and the person specification . To apply for this post, please go to www.jobs.lse.ac.uk . If you have any technical queries with applying on the online system, please use the \u201ccontact us\u201d links at the bottom of the LSE Jobs page. Should you have any queries about the role, please email R.Sanchez-De-La-Sierra@lse.ac.uk . The closing date for receipt of applications is 21 October 2026 (23.59 UK time). Regrettably, we are unable to accept any late applications. Apply now Back to search results Research Assistant Job Type: Research Posted: 05/10/2026 Closing date: 21/10/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (BST) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Baroness Baron Doctor Father Lady Lord Miss Mr Mrs Ms Professor Dame Professor Professor Lord Professor Sir Reverend Sir Other Dame Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection statement Create Account Cancel An email has been sent to your email address. Please confirm that your email address is active by clicking the link in the email. Powered by engage|ats Havas People a Havas Company This site is protected by reCAPTCHA. Contact Us - Application Query Terms and Conditions Privacy Policy Cookies Accessibility FAQs"}, "https://jobs.lse.ac.uk/Vacancies/W/4711/0/475070/15539/senior-technical-business-analyst-ai-automation": {"title": "Senior Technical Business Analyst (AI / Automation)", "description": "Senior Technical Business Analyst (AI / Automation) Register Login Back to search results Senior Technical Business Analyst (AI / Automation) LSE is committed to building a diverse, equitable and truly inclusive university Data and Technology Services Senior Technical Business Analyst (AI / Automation) Salary from \u00a353,949 to \u00a362,160 pa inclusive with potential to progress to \u00a369,073 pa inclusive of London allowance This is a fixed term appointment for 3 years. The London School of Economics is a cosmopolitan university situated in the vibrant centre of London that specialises in the study of social sciences. Our Data and Technology Services division provides services to over 14,000 staff and student users. Data and Technology Services (DTS) delivers technology enabled business change with a focus ranging from strategic and operational business outcomes to service improvements of incumbent services. The scope of DTS projects spans from infrastructure technologies and strategic systems to business processes within end user facing services. The postholder will report into the Lead Technical Business Analyst. This is a hands-on role. Key responsibilities include business and technical analysis\u00a0with the AI/Automation team, with the postholder working directly with business and technical stakeholders to understand problems, elicit and challenge requirements, analyse processes and data flows, develop solution options, and translate business needs into clear requirements for technical delivery teams. The role requires the postholder to personally lead requirements elicitation activities, support testing and service transition, and contribute to business change\u00a0required for LSE to maximise\u00a0measurable business\u00a0benefits\u00a0and outcomes. The postholder will be responsible for researching and understating business needs being addressed by the product team, current technology environment, and utilising incoming technology solutions to develop\u00a0solutions and/or\u00a0service(s) that bridge gap between the current and desired states, whilst ensuring the\u00a0team\u00a0is solving the right\u00a0problem with the\u00a0right tools\u00a0and approach. Candidates should have/be: Significant experience in authoring high quality documentation for business analysis activities, including business requirements, options analysis, process design BPMN 2.0 , user stories, test scripts and acceptance criteria for a technical system delivery Able\u00a0to\u00a0gather and\u00a0interpret user requirements and produce\u00a0viable\u00a0user-centric\u00a0solutions\u00a0in accordance with regulatory\u00a0requirements platform governance (e.g. data protection, access controls, environment strategy) and School policies and procedures. Ability to convert business requirements into user stories, use cases, process models (e.g. BPMN), data models and technical specifications, and support solution validation through prototypes or iterative refinement Able to proactively\u00a0identify\u00a0and manage\u00a0risks,\u00a0issues\u00a0and dependencies, proposing effective\u00a0mitigation\u00a0strategies We offer an occupational pension scheme, generous annual leave, hybrid working, and excellent training and development opportunities. For further information about the post, please see the how to apply document , job description and the person specification . To apply for this post, please go to www.jobs.lse.ac.uk . If you have any technical queries with applying on the online system, please use the \u201ccontact us\u201d links at the bottom of the LSE Jobs page. Should you have any queries about the role, please email dts.admin@lse.ac.uk The closing date for receipt of applications is 21 October 2026 (23.59 UK time). Regrettably, we are unable to accept any late applications. Apply now Back to search results Senior Technical Business Analyst (AI / Automation) Job Type: Professional Services Posted: 29/09/2026 Closing date: 21/10/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (BST) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password C