l be responsible for providing advice, guidance and support on a wide range of employee relations issues to allocated departments at the School. You will provide proactive support to your allocated areas, as well as other customers and colleagues of the School. You will be expected to effectively manage and respond to high volume information requests and queries providing accurate responses in line with the expected standards of service, School policy and current employment law. \u00a0To succeed in the role, you will need to develop effective working relationships with staff at all levels across the School and internally within the HR Division. The role holder will provide valuable input in the development and implementation of new policies and procedures and will have opportunity to actively contribute to wider HR initiatives through working groups and feedback requests. The HR Division, is committed to continually improving and enhancing its service to the School and you will be responsible for identifying, sharing ideas and suggestions to help drive this forward. Skills and Experience Previous experience of giving advice and supporting a busy employee relations environment, including advising managers is essential, as well as a good understanding and knowledge of current employment legislation and HR best practice. A strong interest in Human Resources is essential along with good IT skills, familiarity with Microsoft Office (Word, PowerPoint, Excel and Outlook) is crucial, and excellent written and spoken communication skills is also essential to the role. A passion for delivering high-quality customer service is vital, and the ability to take ownership of your workload to plan, prioritise and deliver on time. The HR Division works with electronic employee record and recruitment systems and demonstrable experience of working with these previously is desirable, and previous experience within the Higher Education sector. This is an exciting time for the Human Resources Division. We are currently working on several delivery enhancing projects, to ensure that our service to the School is effective and responsive to feedback. Candidates will be assessed by interview and a short work-based test. We offer an occupational pension scheme, generous annual leave and excellent training and development opportunities. The role follows a hybrid working pattern. For further information about the post, please see the how to apply document , job description and the person specification . If you have any technical queries with applying on the online system, please use the \u201ccontact us\u201d links at the bottom of the LSE Jobs page. Should you have any queries about the role, please email: L.Dokkari@lse.ac.uk The closing date for receipt of applications is 20 October 2026 (23.59 UK time). Regrettably, we are unable to accept any late applications. Apply now Back to search results HR Adviser (part time 0.5FTE) Job Type: Professional Services Posted: 06/10/2026 Closing date: 20/10/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (BST) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Baroness Baron Doctor Father Lady Lord Miss Mr Mrs Ms Professor Dame Professor Professor Lord Professor Sir Reverend Sir Other Dame Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection s