, admissions, and business development. You will lead the planning and delivery of recruitment activity across international, UK and virtual channels; monitor performance against KPIs; and use market insight, application data and partner feedback to guide efforts. You will also manage the recruitment budget, coordinate trips and events, oversee student ambassador activity, and line manage one direct report. We are looking for a self-starter with excellent organisation, communication and stakeholder management skills. You will be confident working with partners and colleagues at different levels, creative in developing recruitment initiatives, and analytical in evaluating their effectiveness. Experience in Higher Education and a genuine interest in the international education market are highly desirable. Candidates should be able to demonstrate the following key attributes: Experience of delivering student recruitment plans and initiatives that achieve results Experience of building and maintaining effective relationships with international partners and working across cultures Strong analytical skills, with the ability to evaluate performance and present data and reports clearly and succinctly Experience of using CRM systems to support recruitment activity and of managing budgets effectively Excellent communication, presentation and stakeholder management skills, with the ability to influence, collaborate and facilitate action Excellent organisation, attention to detail and the ability to manage competing priorities and deadlines The Extended Education division is a successful and commercially focused division. The courses, degrees and diplomas we offer across this diverse and dynamic portfolio provide a significant revenue source for the school, generating critical funds to invest in LSE\u2019s world-leading teaching and research. We offer an occupational pension scheme, generous annual leave and excellent training and development opportunities. This role is based on our central London campus. Flexible working arrangements are supported within the team. To ensure effective collaboration, stakeholder engagement and an excellent student experience, team members are expected to work on campus for a minimum of three days per week. During the Summer School delivery period, when the level of operational activity and on-campus engagement increases, this rises to four days per week. For further information about the post, please see the how to apply document , job description and the person specification . To apply for this post, please go to www.lse.ac.uk/LSEJobs . If you have any technical queries with applying on the online system, please use the \u201ccontact us\u201d links at the bottom of the LSE Jobs page. Should you have any queries about the role, please email Lisa Lind Havdahl ( l.l.havdahl@lse.ac.uk ). The closing date for receipt of applications is Sunday 18 October (23.59 UK time). Regrettably, we are unable to accept any late applications. Apply now Back to search results Partnerships and Student Recruitment Manager Job Type: Professional Services Posted: 29/09/2026 Closing date: 18/10/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (BST) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Baroness Baron Doctor Father Lady Lord Miss Mr Mrs Ms Professor Dame Professor Professor Lord Professor Sir Reverend Sir Other Dame Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols