 we use on our sites. If you do not allow these services, this website may not function properly. Back Button Cookie List Search Icon Filter Icon Clear checkbox label label Apply Cancel Consent Leg.Interest checkbox label label checkbox label label checkbox label label Reject All Confirm My Choices 1 Technical Support Today New Messages Technical Support Chatbot (with creds) a few seconds ago Welcome to Technical Support. Please could you let us know whether you're a candidate or a recruiter? Candidate Recruiter \u26a1 by Freshworks 1"}, "https://jobs.lse.ac.uk/Vacancies/W/4818/0/475870/15539/lse-fellow-in-interdisciplinary-social-science": {"title": "LSE Fellow in Interdisciplinary Social Science", "description": "LSE Fellow in Interdisciplinary Social Science Register Login Back to search results LSE Fellow in Interdisciplinary Social Science LSE is committed to building a diverse, equitable and truly inclusive university LSE100: The LSE Course LSE Fellow in Interdisciplinary Social Science Salary is competitive and no less than \u00a344,143 pa inclusive of London allowance This is a full-time, fixed term appointment for two years with potential to extend for a further eight months This post will commence on 4 January 2027 LSE100, LSE\u2019s flagship interdisciplinary course taken by all first-year undergraduates, is recruiting a creative educator committed to innovative interdisciplinary teaching to join our team. LSE100 is an internationally-recognised, sector-leading course which introduces LSE students to the School\u2019s mission, builds their capacity to tackle complex problems, and explores transformative global challenges. The successful candidate will teach a minimum of eight fortnightly seminar groups (approximately six classroom hours per week) and contribute to the design and development of course materials, while developing their own research agenda. They will join an enthusiastic community of interdisciplinary educators and will have opportunities to collaborate with colleagues both within LSE100 and across LSE. The successful candidate will also perform administrative duties while fostering a supportive and engaging learning environment for LSE100 students. LSE100 offers three themes for students to choose from as their focus of study. In 2026/27, these are: How can we control AI ?, How can we transform our climate futures?, and How can we create a fair society? The ability to demonstrate research-informed interest and expertise in teaching across multiple themes is an asset. For this post, we are looking for individuals who have an interest in teaching on our How can we create a fair society? theme, and whose research interests connect to the topics of social division, cohesion and/or polarisation. Candidates should have completed or be close to completing a PhD in a social science or related discipline. Relevant teaching and assessment experience particularly in an interdisciplinary context, the ability to work closely with and learn from colleagues, and excellent communication and organisational skills, are also essential. The other criteria used in shortlisting for this post can be found in the person specification on LSE\u2019s recruitment system. Please note that at least one of the referees for this application should be someone who has overseen or managed the candidate\u2019s teaching. We offer an occupational pension scheme, generous annual leave, and excellent training and development opportunities. For further information about the post, please see the how to apply document , job description and the person specification. To apply for this post, please go to www.jobs.lse.ac.uk . If you have any technical queries with applying on the online system, please use the \u201ccontact us\u201d links at the bottom of the LSE Jobs page. Should you have any queries about the role, please email LSE100@lse.ac.uk . The closing date for receipt of applications is 8 November 2026 (23.59 UK time). Regrettably, we are unable to accept any late applications. Interviews are expected to take place on the LSE campus on 19 and 20 November 2026. An LSE Fellowship is intended to be an entry route\u00a0to an academic career and is deemed by the School to be a career development position.\u00a0 As such,\u00a0applicants who have already been employed as an LSE Fellow for three years in total are not eligible to apply. If you have any queries about this please contact the HR Division. Apply now Back to search results LSE Fellow in Interdisciplinary Social Science Job Type: Teaching Posted: 15/10/2026 Closing date: 08/11/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (GMT) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Baroness Baron Doctor Father Lady Lord Miss Mr Mrs Ms Professor Dame Professor Professor Lord Professor Sir Reverend Sir Other Dame Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection statement Create Account Cancel An email has been sent to your email address. Please confirm that your email address is active by clicking the link in the email. Powered by engage|ats Havas People a Havas Company This site is protected by reCAPTCHA. Contact Us - Application Query Terms and Conditions Privacy Policy Cookies Accessibility FAQs"}, "https://jobs.lse.ac.uk/Vacancies/W/1618/0/475806/15539/research-fellow-policy-technology-data-and-city-government-innovation": {"title": "Research Fellow", "description": "Research Fellow - Policy (Technology, Data and City Government Innovation) Register Login Back to search results Research Fellow - Policy (Technology, Data and City Government Innovation) LSE is committed to building a diverse, equitable and truly inclusive university As an equal opportunities employer strongly committed to equity, diversity and inclusion, we encourage applications from women and people from ethnic minority backgrounds as they are currently under-represented at this level in this area. All appointments will be made on merit or skill and experience relative to the role. LSE Cities Research Fellow \u2013 Policy (Technology, Data and City Government Innovation) - 0.5 FTE Salary is no less than \u00a353,949 per annum and the salary scale can be found on the LSE website Funding is available to support this position until 30 June 2027. It is anticipated that the role will be extended beyond this date. LSE Cities is a dynamic research centre at the London School of Economics and Political Science, dedicated to studying how the world's cities are shaped and transformed. We foster cutting-edge research, convene impactful events, and develop future leaders in urban development. The Technology, Data and City Government Innovation research studio investigates the conditions under which European city governments can transition to AI-first, data-driven digital public institutions. Working closely with Professor Alexander Evans, the post holder will work on the studio's core research programme, conducting qualitative and quantitative research independently and in collaboration with colleagues across LSE Cities and affiliated departments. They will develop and deliver long-term research on existing and evolving urban digital infrastructure, variation across policy domains, and the organisation and governance of these capabilities. Candidates should have a PhD awarded or submitted relating to technology, innovation or urban leadership, ideally with a policy focus;\u00a0advanced research skills, including on policy and academic projects; as well as an\u00a0understanding of public sector leadership, administration, data, technology and policy delivery. The other criteria that will be used when shortlisting for this post can be found on the person specification, which is attached to this vacancy on the LSE\u2019s online recruitment system. In addition to a competitive salary the benefits that come with this job include an occupational pension scheme, a research grants policy with personal reward options, generous research leave (sabbatical) entitlement, a collegial faculty environment and excellent support, training and development opportunities. For further information about the post, please see the how to apply document , job description and the person specification. To apply for this post, please go to www.jobs.lse.ac.uk . If you have any technical queries with applying on the online system, please use the \u201ccontact us\u201d links at the bottom of the LSE Jobs page. Should you have any queries about the role, please email Lse.Cities@lse.ac.uk . The closing date for receipt of applications is 8 November 2026 (23.59 UK time). W e are unable to accept any late applications. Apply now Back to search results Research Fellow - Policy (Technology, Data and City Government Innovation) Job Type: Research Posted: 15/10/2026 Closing date: 08/11/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (GMT) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Baroness Baron Doctor Father Lady Lord Miss Mr Mrs Ms Professor Dame Professor Professor Lord Professor Sir Reverend Sir Other Dame Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection statement Create Account Cancel An email has been sent to your email address. Please confirm that your email address is active by clicking the link in the email. Powered by engage|ats Havas People a Havas Company This site is protected by reCAPTCHA. Contact Us - Application Query Terms and Conditions Privacy Policy Cookies Accessibility FAQs"}, "https://jobs.lse.ac.uk/Vacancies/W/5017/0/475742/15539/senior-technical-business-analyst-and-tester": {"title": "Senior Technical Business Analyst and Tester", "description": "Senior Technical Business Analyst and Tester Register Login Back to search results Senior Technical Business Analyst and Tester LSE is committed to building a diverse, equitable and truly inclusive university Academic Registrar\u2019s Division (ARD) Senior Technical Business Analyst and Tester (14 month fixed-term contract or secondment opportunity) Salary from \u00a359,949 to \u00a368,160 pa inclusive with a potential to progress to \u00a375,073 pa inclusive of London allowance (inclusive of a market supplement of \u00a36,000 pa which is periodically reviewed) We are seeking a Senior Technical Business Analyst and Tester to join the ARD Systems team and help deliver and enhance a variety of solutions centred primarily around Salesforce and Marketing Cloud for our Lifelong Learning Service. ARD Systems is the largest Business Led Technology team at LSE, and the largest IT development group Schoolwide. The team are responsible for three of the School\u2019s main platforms, the Student Records System, SITS; the marketing platform, Marketing Cloud; and the enterprise platform, Salesforce.\u00a0The work of the team underpins the day to day running of the School, and the School\u2019s strategy, with the enterprise Salesforce platform a key enabler to much of the strategies successful delivery. The postholder will lead a user experience and quality assurance centric approach to converting business requirements to artefacts required to enable project delivery and continuous improvement. You will have extensive experience of either business analysis, testing analysis or both in the context of large scale business systems change.\u00a0 You will also have excellent interpersonal skills including problem solving and excellent communication skills.\u00a0 Experience of SITS, Salesforce, and the Agile methodology are desirable. We offer an occupational pension scheme, generous annual leave, hybrid working and excellent training and development opportunities. For further information about the post, please see the how to apply document , job description and the person specification . To apply for this post, please go to www.jobs.lse.ac.uk . If you have any technical queries with applying on the online system, please use the \u201ccontact us\u201d links at the bottom of the LSE Jobs page. Should you have any queries about the role, please email Mike Page on m.page@lse.ac.uk The closing date for receipt of applications is 01 November 2026 (23.59 UK time). Regrettably, we are unable to accept any late applications. Apply now Back to search results Senior Technical Business Analyst and Tester Job Type: Professional Services Posted: 14/10/2026 Closing date: 01/11/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (GMT) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend.