ntment for two years The London\nSchool of Economics is a cosmopolitan university situated in the vibrant centre\nof London that specialises in the study of social sciences.\n\u00a0\nLSE\u2019s Data and\nTechnology Services division provides services to over 10,000 staff and student\nusers. The\u00a0DevOps\u00a0Lead\u00a0will\u00a0play\u00a0a\u00a0key\u00a0role\u00a0in\u00a0supporting\u00a0the\u00a0delivery\u00a0of\u00a0the\u00a0LFY\u00a0Programme\u00a0and\u00a0associated\ninitiatives, combining hands-on engineering\nexpertise with leadership of a small team of DevOps\nand\u00a0DataOps\u00a0engineers working across projects and products. Working within the newly established Engineering\nfunction, the role will collaborate closely with the Head of Engineering,\nPlatforms, Networks, Security, Architecture and Delivery Leads to adopt\nexisting operational and engineering standards into project and product\ndelivery, while introducing modern DevOps practices where needed. The postholder will act as a bridge between\noperational services and project/product delivery teams, helping ensure\ninfrastructure, automation, deployment and support requirements are designed\nand delivered in a way that is scalable, secure, reliable and supportable. The\nrole will provide additional technical leadership and coordination while the\nEngineering function evolves and matures. Candidates should have: - Strong knowledge of AWS and/or Azure cloud platforms, including experience supporting hybrid environments spanning public cloud and on-premise infrastructure. - Strong experience with Infrastructure as Code and configuration management technologies such as Terraform, CloudFormation, Ansible or equivalent. - Strong experience building and maintaining CI/CD pipelines using GitLab CI/CD, GitHub Actions, Jenkins, Ansible or equivalent technologies. We offer an occupational pension scheme, generous annual leave, hybrid working, and excellent training and development opportunities. For further information about the post, please see the how to apply document , job description and the person specification. To apply for this post, please go to www.jobs.lse.ac.uk . If you have any technical queries with applying on the online system, please use the \u201ccontact us\u201d links at the bottom of the LSE Jobs page. Should you have any queries about the role, please email dts.admin@lse.ac.uk . The closing date for receipt of applications is 20 October 2026 (23.59 UK time). Regrettably, we are unable to accept any late applications. Apply now Back to search results DevOps Lead Job Type: Professional Services Posted: 13/10/2026 Closing date: 20/10/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (BST) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Baroness Baron Doctor Father Lady Lord Miss Mr Mrs Ms Professor Dame Professor Professor Lord Professor Sir Reverend Sir Other Dame Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection statement Create Account Cancel An email has been sent to your email address. Please confirm that your email address is active by clicking the link in the email. Powered by engage|ats Havas People a Havas Company This site is protected by reCAPTCHA. Contact Us - Application Query Terms and Conditions Privacy Policy Cookies Accessibility FAQs By clicking \u201cAccept All Cookies\u201d, you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to enhance site navigation, analyze site usage, and assist in our marketing efforts. View our privacy policy Cookies Settings Reject All Accept All Cookies Privacy Preference Center When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. This information might be about you, your preferences or your device and is mostly used to make the site work as you expect it to. The information does not usually directly identify you, but it can give you a more personalized web experience. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. Click on the different category headings to find out more and change our default settings. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Allow All Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Services Always Active These Services are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. Functional Services Functional Services With these services, the website is able to provide advanced functionality and personalization. They may be set by us or by third parties whose services we use on our sites. If you do not allow these services, this website may not function properly. Back Button Cookie List Search Icon Filter Icon Clear checkbox label label Apply Cancel Consent Leg.Interest checkbox label label checkbox label label checkbox label label Reject All Confirm My Choices 1 Technical Support Today New Messages Technical Support Chatbot (with creds) a few seconds ago Welcome to Technical Support. Please could you let us know whether you're a candidate or a recruiter? Candidate Recruiter \u26a1 by Freshworks 1"}, "https://jobs.lse.ac.uk/Vacancies/W/4834/0/475869/15539/lse-fellow-in-interdisciplinary-gender-studies": {"title": "LSE Fellow in Interdisciplinary Gender Studies", "description": "LSE Fellow in Interdisciplinary Gender Studies Register Login Back to search results LSE Fellow in Interdisciplinary Gender Studies LSE is committed to building a diverse, equitable and truly inclusive university Department of Gender Studies LSE Fellow in Interdisciplinary Gender Studies Salary from \u00a343,277 to \u00a351,714 pa inclusive with potential to progress to \u00a355,497 pa inclusive of London allowance This is a career development\nposition and is fixed term for two years beginning January 2027. An LSE Fellowship is\nintended to be an entry route\u00a0to an academic career and is deemed by the\nSchool to be a career development position.\u00a0 As such,\u00a0applicants who\nhave already been employed as a LSE Fellow for three years in total are not\neligible to apply. If you have any queries about this please contact the HR\nDivision. The Department of Gender\nStudies addresses the major intellectual challenges posed by contemporary\nchanges in gender relations around the globe and is the largest research and\nteaching unit of its kind in Europe. Academic staff come from a range of disciplinary\nbackgrounds, but we are united in our commitment to mapping and intervening in\nthe gendered nature of social processes, and in our belief that an integrated\ninterdisciplinary and global approach is needed to do so. In our research and\nteaching we combine theory and practice, with an interdisciplinary and\ntransnational perspective. We are looking to recruit an LSE Fellow\nto contribute to teaching and course convening the Department\u2019s\nMSc-level core courses on MSc\nGender and MSc Gender, Development and Globalisation degrees. They will offer\nother MSc level teaching as deemed appropriate by the Head of Department. An\nLSE Fellow post presents an excellent starting point for an early career\nacademic to gain teaching experience while developing their research career. Candidates should have: Completed or close to completing a PhD\n    in social sciences, humanities or an area otherwise related to the teaching\n    needs of the post, by the start date A very good knowledge of interdisciplinary gender scholarship including in\n    areas of gender theories with expertise in any of the following areas:\n    Critical, feminist and decolonial approaches to gender, development, and\n    globalisation; Environment and climate change; Transformation of labour\n    markets, work, employment, and livelihoods; Critical approaches to global\n    development challenges, such as land, food security, health, poverty,\n    technology, urbanisation; Politics of development organisations and/or global\n    governance in development. In addition, knowledge of the following is\nessential: Anti-colonial, anti-imperial, and decolonial approaches to Gender Studies Black feminist and intersectional epistemologies and methodologies Transnational feminist theories and methodologies A developing research record in interdisciplinary gender studies with a substantive focus on areas such as\n    international development, political economy of development, government,\n    politics, social policy or sociology, critical approaches to Artificial\n    Intelligence. We offer an occupational pension scheme, generous annual leave and excellent training and development opportunities. For further information about the post, please see the how to apply document , job description and the person specification. To apply for this post, please go to www.jobs.lse.ac.uk . If you have any technical queries with applying on the online system, please use the \u201ccontact us\u201d links at the bottom of the LSE Jobs page. Should you have any queries about the role, please email gender.manager@lse.ac.uk . The closing date for receipt of applications is 22 November 2026 (23.59 UK time). Regrettably, we are unable to accept any late applications. Apply now Back to search results LSE Fellow in Interdisciplinary Gender Studies Job Type: Teaching Posted: 19/10/2026 Closing date: 22/11/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (GMT) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Baroness Baron Doctor Father Lady Lord Miss Mr Mrs Ms Professor Dame Professor Professor Lord Professor Sir Reverend Sir Other Dame Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection statement Create Account Cancel An email has been sent to your email address. Please confirm that your email address is active by clicking the link in the email. Powered by engage|ats Havas People a Havas Company This site is protected by reCAPTCHA. Contact Us - Application Query Terms and Conditions Privacy Policy Cookies Accessibility FAQs"}, "https://jobs.lse.ac.uk/Vacancies/W/5991/0/476036/15539/employer-relations-manager-12-month-maternity-cover-contract": {"title": "Employer Relations Manager (12 month maternity cover contract)", "description": "Employer Relations Manager (12 month maternity cover contract) Register Login Back to search results Employer Relations Manager (12 month maternity cover contract) LSE is committed to building a diverse, equitable and truly inclusive university Department of Management Employer Relations Manager (12 month maternity cover contract) Salary from \u00a344,143 to \u00a352,749 pa inclusive with potential to progress to \u00a356,607 pa inclusive of London allowance The Department of Management is seeking a dynamic self-starter to join the Careers, Alumni, and Employer Relations (CAER) team, to build upon our programme of corporate and employer engagement activity. We are the largest department in the School, with over 70 faculty, 50 professional services staff and associated guest lecturers and teachers. The Department has over 400 UG students, 800 MSc students, 30 PhD students and 150 Executive students . More information about our programmes is available at: www.lse.ac.uk/management/programmes . By developing relationships with an impressive portfolio of global organisations, we create meaningful opportunities for our students and staff to engage with the business world, contributing to our commitment to drive positive change in business and society. As Employer Relations Manager, you will develop and deliver integrated activities to connect organisations with our programmes, faculty and students , including on-campus events, company visits and calls. You will build long-lasting mutually beneficial partnerships and manage relationships with over 70+ multinational companies and NGOs, and in close partnership with the CEMS double degree programme. You will work be part of the Careers, Alumni, and Employer Relations (CAER) team within the Department of Management, closely with colleagues in multi-functional teams across the department and the School . This is a busy but exciting role that will require someone with outstanding relationship management and support skills. You will need to demonstrate previous experience working in a corporate relations, employer engagement, business development role or related area. Additionally, excellent communication and networking skills; and the ability to initiate projects are key to this role. You\u2019ll need to be strategically-focused , and be confident in using data and market insights to inform your decisions. We offer an occupational pension scheme, generous annual leave, hybrid working, and excellent training and development opportunities. For further information about the post, please see the how to apply document , job description and the person specification . To apply for this post, please go to www.jobs.lse.ac.uk . If you have any technical queries with applying on the online system, please use the \u201ccontact us\u201d links at the bottom of the LSE Jobs page. Should you have any queries about the role, please email Hiba Dabis at h.d.charlton@lse.ac.uk. The closing date for receipt of applications is 15 November 2026 (23.59 UK time). Regrettably, we are unable to accept any late applications. Interviews will take place on campus at LSE on Thursday 26 November 2026. Apply now Back to search results Employer Relations Manager (12 month maternity cover contract) Job Type: Professional Services Posted: 20/10/2026 Closing date: 15/11/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (GMT) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Baroness Baron Doctor Father Lady Lord Miss Mr Mrs Ms Professor Dame Professor Professor Lord Professor Sir Reverend Sir Other Dame Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection statement Create Account Cancel An email has been sent to your email address. Please confirm that your email address is active by clicking the link in the email. Powered by engage|ats Havas People a Havas Company This site is protected by reCAPTCHA. Contact Us - Application Query Terms and Conditions Privacy Policy Cookies Accessibility FAQs By clicking \u201cAccept All Cookies\u201d, you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to enhance site navigation, analyze site usage, and assist in our marketing efforts. View our privacy policy Cookies Settings Reject All Accept All Cookies Privacy Preference Center When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. This information might be about you, your preferences or your device and is mostly used to make the site work as you expect it to. The information does not usually directly identify you, but it can give you a more personalized web experience. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. Click on the different category headings to find out more and change our default settings. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Allow All Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Services Always Active These Services are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. Functional Services Functional Services With these services, the website is able to provide