environmental performance data, contribute to ISO 14001 and ISO 50001 compliance, and support engagement and behaviour change initiatives. The post holder must be flexible because there is a requirement to support activities outside of normal working hours during busy periods such as move-out weekends and graduation. The post holder should have: Experience coordinating operational sustainability activities, such as waste management, sustainable travel, carbon reporting, or resource efficiency, ideally in a higher education, estates, or facilities management environment Understanding of environmental management systems, standards, and legislation, including ISO 14001, ISO 50001, and Duty of Care requirements for waste Experience maintaining and analysing environmental performance data, with the ability to produce accurate management information for internal and external reporting (e.g. SECR, HESA, EMR) Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to engage effectively with a wide range of stakeholders including contractors, staff, and students Strong organisational skills and attention to detail, with the ability to manage multiple workstreams, prioritise effectively, and maintain accurate compliance records We offer an occupational pension scheme, generous annual leave, hybrid working and excellent training and development opportunities. For further information about the post, please see\u00a0the how to apply document , job description and the person specification . To apply for this post, please go to www.jobs.lse.ac.uk . If you have any technical queries with applying on the online system, please use the \u201ccontact us\u201d links at the bottom of the LSE Jobs page. Should you have any queries about the role, please email s.van-de-pette@lse.ac.uk The closing date for receipt of applications is 15 th November 2026 (23.59 UK time). Regrettably, we are unable to accept any late applications. Apply now Back to search results Sustainable Operations Officer Job Type: Professional Services Posted: 23/10/2026 Closing date: 15/11/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (GMT) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Baroness Baron Doctor Father Lady Lord Miss Mr Mrs Ms Professor Dame Professor Professor Lord Professor Sir Reverend Sir Other Dame Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection statement Create Account Cancel An email has been sent to your email address. Please confirm that your email address is active by clicking the link in the email. Powered by engage|ats Havas People a Havas Company This site is protected by reCAPTCHA. Contact Us - Application Query Terms and Conditions Privacy Policy Cookies Accessibility FAQs By clicking \u201cAccept All Cookies\u201d, you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to enhance site navigation, analyze site usage, and assist in our marketing efforts. View our privacy policy Cookies Settings Reject All Accept All Cookies Privacy Preference Center When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. This information might be about you, your preferences or your device and is mostly used to make the site work as you expect it to. The information does not usually directly identify you, but it can give you 