h potential to progress to \u00a370,455 pa inclusive of London allowance Funding is available to support this position for two years, with extension subject to funding. The Centre for Economic Transition Expertise (CETEx) is a policy research centre within the Global School of Sustainability at LSE. CETEx develops independent research, policy analysis, technical assistance and capacity-building programmes that support policymakers, central banks, finance ministries and regulators in delivering sustainable, inclusive and resilient economies and financial systems. By combining academic research with practical policy expertise, CETEx helps decision-makers implement effective climate, nature and economic transition reforms around the world. CETEx is seeking a Policy Fellow to lead an ambitious programme of research and technical support focused on economic and fiscal policy and its interlinkages with monetary and financial-supervisor policymaking in Indonesia and Southeast Asia, with the opportunity to work in other emerging markets and developing economies (EMDEs). CETEx is seeking to appoint a Policy Fellow to work within the EMDEs pillar of the centre, conduct research, develop policies and lead engagements that help policymakers develop and implement policies that accelerate an inclusive, low-carbon and climate-resilient transition. The postholder will employ their reputation for rigorous policy-related research and related activities at a senior level to ensure that research outputs have demonstrable impact and inform policy debates and decision. The postholder will have a postgraduate degree in finance, economics, climate/environmental governance, environmental/ecological economics, public/social policy or a closely related field, and hold experience working closely with or within a fiscal, monetary or economic policymaker such as a finance ministry, central bank, financial regulator, or a public finance institution, preferably on environmental risks or opportunities or other sustainability challenges. Furthermore, the postholder will have excellent and demonstrable understanding of the impact of environmental risks and opportunities on macroeconomic variables such as GDP, employment, prices, fiscal revenues, fiscal expenditure, debt sustainability and broader macroeconomic stability measures. Experience working on environment-related policy issues in Southeast Asia, with Indonesia in focus, and Excellent understanding of public finance and fiscal policy levers that can be used to support a low-carbon and climate-resilient transition, such as blended finance mechanisms, carbon taxes and credits, tax breaks and subsidies and other (dis)incentives, with broader fiscal \u2013 monetary interlinkage are essential in this role. We offer an occupational pension scheme, generous annual leave, hybrid working, and excellent training and development opportunities. For further information about the post, please see the how to apply document , job description and the person specification. To apply for this post, please go to www.jobs.lse.ac.uk . If you have any technical queries with applying on the online system, please use the \u201ccontact us\u201d links at the bottom of the LSE Jobs page. Should you have any queries about the role, please email gri.hr@lse.ac.uk The closing date for receipt of applications is Sunday 8 November 2026 (23.59 UK time). Regrettably, Apply now Back to search results Policy Fellow (Southeast Asia) Job Type: Policy Posted: 21/10/2026 Closing date: 08/11/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (GMT) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Baroness Baron Doctor Father Lady Lord Miss Mr Mrs Ms Professor Dame Professor Professor Lord Professor Sir Reverend Sir Other Dame Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection statement Create Account Cancel An email has been sent to your email address. Please confirm that your email address is active by clicking the link in the email. Powered by engage|ats Havas People a Havas Company This site is protected by reCAPTCHA. Contact Us - Application Query Terms and Conditions Privacy Policy Cookies Accessibility FAQs"}, "https://jobs.lse.ac.uk/Vacancies/W/6869/0/470234/15539/student-lifecycle-programme-officer": {"title": "Student Lifecycle Programme Officer", "description": "Student Lifecycle Programme Officer Register Login Back to search results Student Lifecycle Programme Officer LSE is committed to building a diverse, equitable and truly inclusive university Student\nCommunities, Student Learning and Personal Development Student Lifecycle Programme Officer Salary from \u00a344,143 to \u00a0\u00a352,749 pa, with potential to progress to\u00a0 \u00a356,607 pa inclusive of London allowance Fixed-term appointment until 31 July 2029 The role You will coordinate LSE Navigate, a network and programme\nof activity to support students who have received a contextual offer,\nthroughout their whole journey, from receiving an offer through to post-graduation.\nWorking with teams across LSE, you will bring together the development,\nimplementation and evaluation of this pilot initiative, aiming to provide\nequitable access to academic, personal and professional opportunities and\nsupport services. You will work closely with operational roles delivering\nactivities, support the strategic project board, and collaborate with\ncolleagues and students to evolve LSE Navigate. The team and wider context The postholder will be directly responsible for\nactivities in the access and on-course stages of the student lifecycle, based\nin the Student Communities Team with a dotted-line reporting link to the\nWidening Participation Team. This innovative project is a key element of our Access\nand Participation Plan and contributes to the School\u2019s strategy, LSE2030 \u2013\nEducate for Global Impact strand, to improve equality of opportunity for\nstudents from disadvantaged and underrepresented backgrounds. What we\u2019re looking for We\u2019re looking for someone with the ability to lead operational\ndevelopment and delivery in order to deliver on our strategic objectives.\nEssential skills and experience include: Experience\n    of managing projects and/or relationships with multiple stakeholders and\n    contributors Knowledge\n    or interest in the UK higher education sector; and widening participation\n    issues Experience\n    of consulting service users or project beneficiaries to gather feedback and\n    inform continuous improvement Ability to work and communicate\n    with people at all levels including current students, university applicants,\n    academic staff, senior stakeholders and external funders What LSE has to offer LSE is one of the world\u2019s leading institutions for the\nstudy of the social sciences. With 18 Nobel Prize winners, 37 past or present\nheads of state and ranking among the top 50 universities in the world (QS\n2024), we are a truly international university at the forefront of global\npolicy debate. We offer an occupational pension scheme, generous annual\nleave, hybrid working, and excellent training and development opportunities. This position is subject to an enhanced Disclosure and\nBarring Service (DBS) check with children\u2019s barred list. Any offer of\nemployment made is conditional on receipt of a satisfactory DBS check. For further information about\nthe post, please see the how to apply document , job description and the person specification . How\nto apply: To apply for this post, please go to www.jobs.lse.ac.uk. P lease outline how you meet the criteria in the\n    person specification in your application. The closing date for receipt of applications is Sunday\n8 November 2026 (23.59 UK time). Regrettably, we are unable to accept any late\napplications. The first round of interviews are scheduled to\ntake place on 18 November (online). The second round of interviews are\nscheduled to take place on 25 November (in person). If you have any technical queries with applying on the online system,\nplease use the \u201ccontact us\u201d links at the bottom of the LSE Jobs page. Should\nyou have any queries about the role, please email Dr Emma Bates (Student\nCommunities Lead): e.bates1@lse.ac.uk Apply now Back to search results Student Lifecycle Programme Officer Job Type: Professional Services Posted: 23/10/2026 Closing date: 08/11/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (GMT) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Baroness Baron Doctor Father Lady Lord Miss Mr Mrs Ms Professor Dame Professor Professor Lord Professor Sir Reverend Sir Other Dame Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection statement Create Account Cancel An email has been sent to your email address. Please confirm that your email address is active by clicking the link in the email. Powered by engage|ats Havas People a Havas Company This site is protected by reCAPTCHA. Contact Us - Application Query Terms and Conditions Privacy Policy Cookies Accessibility FAQs By clicking \u201cAccept All Cookies\u201d, you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to enhance site navigation, analyze site usage, and assist in our marketing efforts. View our privacy policy Cookies Settings Reject All Accept All Cookies Privacy Preference Center When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. This information might be about you, your preferences or your device and is mostly used to make the site work as you expect it to. The information does not usually directly identify you, but it can give you a more personalized web experience. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. Click on the different category headings to find out more and change our default settings. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Allow All Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Services Always Active These Services are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. Functional Services Functional Services With these services, the website is able to provide advanced functionality and personalization. They may be set by us or by third parties whose services we use on our sites. If you do not allow these services, this website may not function properly. Back Button Cookie List Search Icon Filter Icon Clear checkbox label label Apply Cancel Consent Leg.Interest checkbox label label checkbox label label checkbox label label Reject All Confirm My Choices 1 Technical Support Today New Messages Technical Support Chatbot (with creds) a few seconds ago Welcome to Technical Support. Please could you let us know whether you're a candidate or a recruiter? Candidate Recruiter \u26a1 by Freshworks 1"}, "https://jobs.lse.ac.uk/Vacancies/W/7028/0/476169/15539/study-abroad-coordinator-admissions": {"title": "Study Abroad Coordinator (Admissions)", "description": "Study Abroad Coordinator (Admissions) Register Login Back to search results Study Abroad Coordinator (Admissions) LSE is committed to building a diverse, equitable and truly inclusive university Study Abroad Coordinator (Admissions) Student Recruitment and Study Abroad:\nRecruitment and Admissions Salary from \u00a337,244 to \u00a342,397 per annum inclusive with potential to progress to \u00a345,358 pa inclusive of London allowance This is a fixed term appointment for 12 months The London School of Economics and Political Science (LSE) is one of the world\u2019s leading institutions for the study of the social sciences. With 20 Nobel Prize winners, 37 past or present heads of state and ranking among the top 50 universities in the world (QS 2024), LSE is a truly international university at the forefront of global policy debate. The Student Recruitment and Study Abroad team has primary responsibility for: Student recruitment: both UK and international, for undergraduate, graduate and study abroad programmes. The General Course: all pre-arrival and social aspects of the School\u2019s year-long inbound study abroad programme. Global Opportunities (GO) LSE: all student facing aspects of the School\u2019s reciprocal student exchange programme. The Study Abroad Coordinator (Admissions) has day-to-day responsibility for all aspects of the admissions process for the School\u2019s two study abroad programmes, the General Course and GO LSE. They deliver high-quality experience to applicants, partner institutions and internal stakeholders and produce management information that supports promotion, recruitment and enrolment. They also represent the School at recruitment events (undergraduate and graduate) on and off campus Candidates must have: Experience of successfully managing a complex and demanding professional workload whilst maintaining impeccable attention to detail. Ability to work proactively and with limited supervision. Confidence in making reasoned independent decisions that comply with agreed criteria. We offer an occupational pension scheme, generous annual leave, hybrid working, and excellent training and development opportunities. For further information about the post, please see the how to apply document , job description and the person specification . To apply for this post, please go to www.jobs.lse.ac.uk . If you have any technical queries with applying on the online system, please use the \u201ccontact us\u201d links at the bottom of the LSE Jobs page. Should you have any queries about the role, please email Rachel Davies-English at r.b.davies-english@lse.ac.uk The closing date for receipt of applications is Friday 6 th November 2026 (23.59 UK time). Regrettably, we are unable to accept any late applications. Interviews are likely to be held the week commencing 16 th November 2026. This position will be subject to an enhanced Disclosure and Barring Service (DBS) check. Any offer of employment made is conditional on receipt of a satisfactory DBS check. Apply now Back to search results Study Abroad Coordinator (Admissions) Job Type: Professional Services Posted: 22/10/2026 Closing date: 06/11/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (GMT) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Baroness Baron Doctor Father Lady Lord Miss Mr Mrs Ms Professor Dame Professor Professor Lord Professor Sir Reverend Sir Other Dame Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection statement Create Account Cancel An email has been sent to your email address. Please confirm that your email address is active by clicking the link in the email. Powered by engage|ats Havas People a Havas Company This site is protected by reCAPTCHA. Contact Us - Application Query Terms and Conditions Privacy Policy Cookies Accessibility FAQs"}, "https://jobs.lse.ac.uk/Vacancies/W/7115/0/476038/15539/data-and-insight-assistant": {"title": "Data and Insight Assistant", "description": "Data and Insight Assistant Register Login Back to search results Data and Insight Assistant LSE is committed to building a diverse, equitable and truly inclusive university LSE Careers Data and Insight Assistant Salary from \u00a333,548 to \u00a336,774 pa inclusive with potential to progress to \u00a339,191 pa inclusive of London allowance This is a fixed term appointment to 31 July 2027 LSE Careers is dedicated to supporting our students and recent alumni in all aspects of their career planning and professional development. Offering an extensive programme of events and activities to help them develop the skills and knowledge they need to succeed, we are committed to delivering work to a high professional standard and continually enhancing and developing the services we offer. The Data and Insight Assistant will support LSE Careers to make effective use of data and insight to understand student, alumni and employer engagement, needs and outcomes and to inform service planning, delivery and continuous improvement. The post-holder will support the development and maintenance of LSE Careers\u2019 reporting and insight provision, bringing together data from the customer relationship management (CRM) system and other relevant sources to produce accessible, accurate and timely reporting and analysis. We are looking for someone with experience of working with quantitative data and producing accurate analysis, with strong Excel skills and an understanding of good practice in preparing and analysing data. You will be able to identify patterns and trends and communicate findings clearly through reports, visualisations and concise commentary for non-specialist audiences. You will also be a collaborative and organised colleague, able to build effective working relationships, manage competing priorities and contribute to high-quality data and reporting activity. We offer an occupational pension scheme, generous annual leave, hybrid working and excellent training and development opportunities. The post-holder would be expected to be on campus at least three days per week. For further information about the post, please see the how to apply document , job description and the person specification . To apply for this post, please go to www.jobs.lse.ac.uk . If you have any technical queries with applying on the online system, please use the \u201ccontact us\u201d links at the bottom of the LSE Jobs page. Should you have any queries about the role, please email the LSE Careers team at careers.seo@lse.ac.uk . The closing date for receipt of applications is 5 November 2026 (23.59 UK time). Interviews will take place 10 November 2026. Regrettably, we are unable to accept any late applications. Apply now Back to search results Data and Insight Assistant Job Type: Professional Services Posted: 20/10/2026 Closing date: 05/11/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (GMT) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Baroness Baron Doctor Father Lady Lord Miss Mr Mrs Ms Professor Dame Professor Professor Lord Professor Sir Reverend Sir Other Dame Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection statement Create Account Cancel An email has been sent to your email address. Please confirm that your email address is active by clicking the link in the email. Powered by engage|ats Havas People a Havas Company This site is protected by reCAPTCHA. Contact Us - Application Query Terms and Conditions Privacy Policy Cookies Accessibility FAQs"}, "https://jobs.lse.ac.uk/Vacancies/W/2071/0/475947/15539/igc-finance-manager": {"title": "IGC Finance Manager", "description": "IGC Finance Manager Register Login Back to search results IGC Finance Manager L SE is committed to building a diverse, equitable and truly inclusive university International Growth Centre Finance Manager \u2013 IGC Salary from \u00a0\u00a344,143 to \u00a352,749 (with potential to progress to \u00a356,607 pa inclusive of London allowance) International Growth Centre works with policymakers in developing countries to promote inclusive and sustainable growth through pathbreaking research. The IGC is a global research centre with a network of world-leading researchers and in-country teams and initiatives working across Africa, South Asia, and the Middle East. Based at LSE and in partnership with the University of Oxford, we are majority funded by the UK Foreign, Commonwealth and Development Office with support from other global funders. We work to improve the productivity of people and firms as the key driver of sustainable economic development. We are seeking a highly motivated and proactive Finance Manager to join our supportive and collaborative Finance and Operations team. The role will lead on management reporting, financial monitoring and the delivery of high-quality finance services across the IGC. Working closely with colleagues across the IGC, country teams and central LSE services, the postholder will support the delivery of effective financial controls, provide high-quality management information, and contribute to the continuous improvement of systems and processes. The role will also provide day-to-day supervision and guidance to a team of Finance and Operations Officers. The successful applicant will have: Strong experience of management accounting, budgeting and forecasting, ideally in a complex or donor-funded environment Excellent attention to detail, analytical and problem-solving skills Strong Excel skills and experience in using financial systems The ability to communicate complex financial information clearly to financial and non-financial stakeholders Strong organisational and interpersonal skills, with the ability to manage competing priorities and build effective relationships across diverse teams and cultures The position will be based in the IGC head office located within the LSE in central London, with flexibility for hybrid work. We offer an occupational pension scheme, generous annual leave, and excellent training and development opportunities. For further information about the post, please see the how to apply document , job description and the person specification . To apply for this post, please go to: https://jobs.lse.ac.uk/ .If you have any technical queries with applying on the online system, please use the \u201ccontact us\u201d links at the bottom of the LSE Jobs page. Should you have any queries about the role, please email Arinder Sidhu, IGC Head of Finance and Operations at: a.sidhu@lse.ac.uk . To find out more about the IGC, please go to www.theigc.org/about/careers . The closing date for receipt of applications is 2 November 2026 \u00a0(23.59 UK time). Regrettably, we are unable to accept any late applications. Interviews will be held as soon as possible thereafter. Apply now Back to search results IGC Finance Manager Job Type: Professional Services Posted: 19/10/2026 Closing date: 02/11/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (GMT) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Baroness Baron Doctor Father Lady Lord Miss Mr Mrs Ms Professor Dame Professor Professor Lord Professor Sir Reverend Sir Other Dame Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection statement Create Account Cancel An email has been sent to your email address. Please confirm that your emai